BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 50 760 Td (Warm-up: Fibonacci numbers) Tj T* () Tj T* (The Fibonacci numbers are defined by F\(0\) = 0, F\(1\) = 1, and F\(n\) = F\(n-1\) + F\(n-2\) for n) Tj T* (of 2 or more.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The naive recursive function that follows this definition directly is very slow. Computing) Tj T* (F\(n\) calls F\(n-1\) and F\(n-2\), and F\(n-1\) calls F\(n-2\) again, so the same values are) Tj T* (recomputed over and over. The number of calls grows exponentially, roughly as 1.618 to the) Tj T* (power n. Computing F\(50\) this way makes over twenty billion calls.) Tj T* () Tj T* (With memoization we store each F\(k\) the first time it is computed. Every value from F\(0\)) Tj T* (to F\(n\) is then computed exactly once, so the running time drops to O\(n\), using O\(n\) extra) Tj T* (space for the table.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The bottom-up version fills an array from index 0 upward. Because each entry depends only) Tj T* (on the previous two, we do not need the whole array: two variables are enough. That) Tj T* (reduces the space from O\(n\) to O\(1\) while keeping the O\(n\) running time.) Tj T* () Tj T* (The lesson of the warm-up is the question to ask of every dynamic program: what exactly is) Tj T* (the subproblem, and in what order can the table be filled?) Tj T* ET
endstream
endobj
