BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 50 760 Td (Summary and common mistakes) Tj T* () Tj T* (A recipe for designing a dynamic program:) Tj T* (1. Define the subproblem precisely, in words, including what each index means.) Tj T* (2. Write the recurrence that relates a subproblem to smaller ones.) Tj T* (3. State the base cases.) Tj T* (4. Choose a fill order in which dependencies are computed first.) Tj T* (5. Say where the final answer is in the table.) Tj T* (6. Analyze the running time as the number of subproblems times the work per subproblem.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Common mistakes seen on past exams:) Tj T* (- Stating a recurrence without defining what the table entry means. This loses most of the) Tj T* (credit even if the recurrence is right.) Tj T* (- Forgetting the base cases, or indexing the strings from 0 in one place and from 1 in) Tj T* (another.) Tj T* (- Filling the knapsack row from left to right in the one-row version, which lets an item) Tj T* (be taken more than once and solves the unbounded knapsack problem instead.) Tj T* (- Claiming the knapsack algorithm runs in polynomial time.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Next lecture covers edit distance and matrix chain multiplication. Read sections 15.2 and) Tj T* (15.5 of the textbook before class.) Tj T* ET
endstream
